          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.1.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.283,
            0.424,
            0.334
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Rihan marked a point on a piece of paper. How many lines can he draw that pass through the point?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.468,
            0.287,
            0.765,
            0.354
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Sheetal marked two points on a piece of paper. How many different lines can she draw that pass through both of the points?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.37,
            0.572,
            0.388
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you help Rihan and Sheetal find their answers?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.398,
            0.794,
            0.442
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. Rihan can draw many/uncountable number of lines through the given point. Sheetal can draw only one line through the two given points."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.451,
            0.88,
            0.487
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.2. Name the line segments in Fig. 2.4. Which of the five marked points are on exactly one of the line segments? Which are on two of the line segments?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.49,
            0.33,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { L } \\overline { { \\mathbf { M } } } , \\overline { { \\mathbf { M } } } \\overline { { \\mathbf { P } } } , \\overline { { \\mathbf { P } } } \\overline { { \\mathbf { Q } } } , \\overline { { \\mathbf { Q } } } \\overline { { \\mathbf { R } } }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.524,
            0.881,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Points L and R are exactly on one line segment. Points M, P and Q are on two line segments."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.568,
            0.825,
            0.599
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.3. Name the rays shown in Fig. 2.5. Is T the starting point of each of these rays?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\begin{array} { r l } { \\rightarrow \\rightarrow \\rightarrow } & { { } \\rightarrow } \\end{array}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.595,
            0.357,
            0.612
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. TA, TB, TN and NB"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.623,
            0.668,
            0.641
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "No, T is the starting point of TB, TN and TA but not of NB."
